 and there's this entire plot/info dump (early on) where we’re told <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="0a6920bc-6280-48ea-8749-c3c4adeec6a2" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="0a6920bc-6280-48ea-8749-c3c4adeec6a2"> years ago Amelia’s mom tried to sell her virginity to someone and she was kidnapped, her sister went undercover in a secret organization called “The Society” to find her and met her Irish mob husband who dismantled it, but someone is still threatening Amelia that they will release a tape of her sister being raped if she tattles on some trafficking dudes. The sis agreed to be raped when she was 17 to save Amelia, and may have been assaulted while she was u/c. For his part, Sante was in an abusive situation and killed his dad and another mobster dude and had to go to Italy. He's related to the head of the Italian mob. It was a lot and told with little explanation like we know what’s going on and who these people are which is why I really think her sister had a book that introduced all these players. </label><br /><br />Sante’s character wasn’t really developed much. He was rich, he spent time in Italy, but what did he do besides follow the h around? I’m not sure he even had a position with the family. Amelia got on my nerves. She whined, kept secrets, made the dumbest decisions, (like walking home after she just escaped a goon), but she grew as the story progressed. I really liked her sister though. <br /><br /><u>Bottom Line</u>- It was ok with skimming. I was lost at times and felt like I wasn’t in the loop. There were large chunks of the book where we were stuck in the same holding pattern. The chemistry wasn’t great, the sexy time wasn’t what I’d call hot, but she’s a SA survivor. Tons of trigger, but no safety concerns. (other than the mention that he got around while he was in Italy the last few years)<br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/80698268?shelf=kindle-unlimited" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">kindle-unlimited</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/80698268?shelf=mobsters" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">mobsters</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/80698268?shelf=stalker" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">stalker</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">17 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">2 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 