 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined0small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8370701831">February 27, 2026</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">3.5 🌟<br /><br />'I’m as helpless as a butterfly trapped in a jar. If the jar was in his hands, would he release me or pluck off my wings as a souvenir? Release doesn’t seem an option for a man like him.' (Ch 9)<br /><br />Devil's Thirst<br />(The Moretti Men Book 1)<br />By Jill Ramsower<br />Narrated by Brooke Daniels &amp; Peter Alden<br />9 hrs 12 mins / 335 Pages<br />ALC/ebook Review<br /><br />Lite Dark Stalker Romance | Mafia Romance | Morally Grey | Touch Her and 💀<br /><br />'Fight or flight— at least those show a person is trying to avoid harm. Then there’s the freeze instinct.' (Ch 13)<br /><br />Was hooked and enthralled with the story. (Except the part where MMC is a hypocrite, ugh. Like, dude, don't you think all of that crap sounds very eerily familiar to what you have done to Amelie... Yet, he never does realize it.)<br /><br />'Nothing about this city is normal, and that’s what makes it epic. Maybe one day the fears will no longer haunt me, and I’ll be epic, too.' (Ch 1)<br /><br />For all the trauma that Amelie went through in the past, she took everything rather well. Perhaps too well. I also didn't wholly buy into the MMC's reasoning behind the things he did to work his way into her life either. But it worked out for them.<br /><br />'He’s also domineering, possessive, and a tiny bit unhinged.<br />....<br />Yeah, but I have my own fun little quirks as well.' (Ch 31)<br /><br />For the ALC, I liked the narrators. Just really prefer not to have the female narrator speak the male parts and the male narrator speak the female parts. For me, personally, it kind of dampened the setting or mood. Also, their pronunciations of Italian words and names were a little cringe. Other than that, it was good.<br /><br />ALC/ebook courtesy of Hambright PR | Jill Ramsower LLC</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">4 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438