dContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I am a sucker for mafia romance and this book delivered! This has so much potential. I liked the plot line. I felt like there was a good amount of story to smut. But there were times when I was getting bored and waiting to Amelie to finally start making sense. <br /><br />I loved how Sante was so possessive and obsessed with Amelie to the point of stalking her for weeks. It sounds messed up but I liked it. LOL he literally stalks her to protect her. I liked how he was so intuitive to Amelie’s feelings and actions. He knew what she needed before she even said anything. <br /><br />I didn’t like how Amelie was keeping all these secrets thinking she couldn’t do anything. Like the only way to protect her and her family was to stay quiet?? She has so many ties to the Irish mafia, the Italian mafia, and the Russian mafia!! All her friends and family are in the mafia!! You’re telling me you couldn’t ask them for help??? Her brother-in-law literally took out The Society that kidnapped her when she was younger and you couldn’t ask him to help you take down this one guy???? It just made no sense to me. <br /><br />Also what was with the revelation about Umberto?? That secret literally did nothing for the storyline. It was seriously pointless. <br /><br />While this is the first book in the series and the first I’ve read from the author, I realized as I was reading the this is an interconnected series with the Byrne brothers series. You can read it as a standalone but I feel like you should read the Byrne brothers series first. There were times where I was lost and confused because I didn’t have the back story. Like the whole thing with The Society. They were mentioned a few times but I don’t even know what they actually were. And they play a big part in Amelie’s past. <br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tag