 class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I was so so so excited about this book when I read the tropes. But it just didn’t come together the way I hoped and that made me sad because I truly love Jill Ramsowers writing and books. <br /><br />In this book we have Sante, our MMC and Amelie, our FMC. They meet at her sisters wedding and sparks fly. But they are both very young…working through serious issues and trauma. And before anything can come of them, Sante is sent to Sicily for 4 years. <br /><br />When he comes back, Amelie is deep into her ballet career and Sante is OTT obsessed with her. To the point that he moves in next door to her she starts to stalk her. She doesn’t even realise it’s him because he’s changed so much in the 4 years he’s been gone. <br /><br />I’ve seen people having issues with the fact that he wasn’t celibate the 4 years he was gone…it wasn’t a big deal. They never had relationship before he left so really even though he had feelings for he the whole time, he was under no obligation to be faithful. It just is what it is. What did bother be was his aggression when it came to $£x. <br /><br />Sante had so many moments of sincerity and caring that truly made my heart melt. But at the same time he was so aggressive when it came to getting her in bed. It felt like that was all he cared about. It just gave me the ick. Because it wasn’t a thing where they were both feeling it. It was 1000000% one sided. She had feelings for him but was still trying to get to know him and he just wanted to get to know her insides 😩😩😩<br /><br />The first half of the book was OK…but the second half felt like a literal time warp. We zoomed so fast through things that I had no idea what was happening. I thought I was missing pages. <br /><br />This one wasn’t a hit for me. But it might be for you so if this is up your alley definitely give it a shot ❤️<br /><br />Thank you so much to Jill Ramsower and Valentine PR for the opportunity to ARC read this book ❤️</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">2 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036344 L9.66834148,18.1034086 C9.31027068,18.6437214 8.696742,19 8,19 L6,19 C4.8954305,19 4,18.1045695 4,17 L4,12 C4,10.8954305 4.8954305,10 6,10 L8,10 C8.60249245,10 9.14276174,10.2664091 9.50943372,10.6878531 L9.58578644,10.6036344 L11,9.18942086 L11,6.75238209 C10.9999468,5.91477784 11.5910613,5.19356674 12.4123594,5.02913493 C13.3640475,4.8385978 14.290004,5.45563256 14.4813282,6.41129383 Z M8,11 L6,11 C5.44771525,11 5,11.4477153 5,12 L5,17 C