dFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7474073802">February 14, 2026</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I received the ALC for this book from Hambright pr and this is my honest review.<br /><br />To start this book is the definition of "He falls first..and hard". The MMC Sante had all the alpha anti-hero Italian vibes with his soft side for his one and only FMC Amelie. I loved the ballerina/mafia style this book brought. While it did have a slow start feeling as if it was dragging out and was difficult in the beginning to emotionally connect with the characters, I did enjoy the satisfying ending and character growth of both the MCs. <br /><br />Brook Daniels did a phenomenal job of narrating the female POV of the book. When she had to read the MMC lines I didn't feel a change or awkwardness like with some audible narrators. I could really hear the emotions in the character and her lines were read with palpable feelings. <br /><br />Peter Aiden did a wonderful job narrating the MMC as well. He really gave that gravel voice a deep sense of yearning that character had and I was 100% here for it. I will say when he read the FMC during his POV it was a bit awkward for me but that could be because I don't listen to audio books very often. <br /><br />Overall I would say I did enjoy this book and if you're looking for a quick read that scratches that insta love/mafia vibes I would suggest this book. </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data