astRevisionAt":1739840155498,"text":"\u003cb\u003e2.5-ish ⭐’s\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI’m so far behind with reviews that I read this two weekends ago and remember very little, so that’s telling. I’m writing this mostly from notes but do remember it being slow at times.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAmelia is a ballet dancer with demons and a stalker when she meets a mysterious stranger that she’s instantly pulled towards. We learn from Sante’s POV that the two met four (I believe) years earlier and he has been hung up on her since. It’s not explained why she doesn’t recognize him, but she doesn’t. Sante is OBSESSED and quickly infiltrates her life, which isn’t all bad because she needs some saving.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI’m not sure if this is a spinoff (because it’s the first book) but it felt like we were dropped into an existing storyline. There’re Italian and Irish mobsters that I felt like we should know, and there's this entire plot/info dump (early on) where we’re told \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"0a6920bc-6280-48ea-8749-c3c4adeec6a2\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"0a6920bc-6280-48ea-8749-c3c4adeec6a2\"\u003e years ago Amelia’s mom tried to sell her virginity to someone and she was kidnapped, her sister went undercover in a secret organization called “The Society” to find her and met her Irish mob husband who dismantled it, but someone is still threatening Amelia that they will release a tape of her sister being raped if she tattles on some trafficking dudes. The sis agreed to be raped when she was 17 to save Amelia, and may have been assaulted while she was u/c. For his part, Sante was in an abusive situation and killed his dad and another mobster dude and had to go to Italy. He's related to the head of the Italian mob. It was a lot and told with little explanation like we know what’s going on and who these people are which is why I really think her sister had a book that introduced all these players. \u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSante’s character wasn’t really developed much. He was rich, he spent time in Italy, but what did he do besides follow the h around? I’m not sure he even had a position with the family. Amelia got on my nerves. She whined, kept secrets, made the dumbest decisions, (like walking home after she just escaped a goon), but she grew as the story progressed. I really liked her sister though. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cu\u003eBottom Line\u003c/u\u003e- It was ok with skimming. I was lost at times and felt like I wasn’t in the loop. There were large chunks of the book where we were stuck in the same holding pattern. The chemistry wasn’t great, the sexy time wasn’t what I’d call hot, but she’s a SA survivor. Tons of trigger, but no safety concerns. (other than the mention that he got around while he was in Italy the last few years)\u003cbr /\u003e","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2DCB4V4V4Y8WT\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz\"}}"},"likeCount":17,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":2},"User:6753356":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":6753356,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1613277139i/6753356._UX200_CR0,14,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":275,"textReviewsCount":805,"name":"Anastasia ｼ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/6753356-anastasia","contributor":null,"id":6753356},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A19R7MNJ1GKII":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A19R7MNJ1GKII"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A19R7MNJ1GKII\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A19R7MNJ1GKII","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A19R7MNJ1GKII"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"4-stars","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=4-stars"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"2024","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=2024"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"arc","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=arc"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"adult","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=adult"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"authors-r","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=authors-r"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"contemporary","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=contemporary"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"dark-romance","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=dark-romance"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"erotica","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=erotica"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"reviewed","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=reviewed"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"romance","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6753356?shelf=romance"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7070985723"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.eDyxuIbfVCnm3eaIjG2XTQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.eDyxuIbfVCnm3eaIjG2XTQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:6753356"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1765349883740,"createdAt":1734563555343,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1765349883740,"text":"╭ ✦ •\u003cbr /\u003e│ ⊹ 𝟺.𝟻 𝚜𝚝𝚊𝚛𝚜, , 𝚏𝚞𝚕𝚕 \u003ca href=\"https://wp.me/p23dZM-5Ps\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003e𝚁𝚎𝚟𝚒𝚎𝚠\u003c/a\u003e 𝚘𝚗 𝚖𝚢 𝚋𝚕𝚘𝚐! ⊹\u003cbr /\u003e╰ ✦ •\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003e“It isn’t going to work, or you’re too scared to try? Because the only issue I see is a scared little girl who’s looking for every excuse she can find to run from the one person putting her first.” \u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWow! Okay, as I was reading this, I wasn't sure how to rate this, but the last 40% was amazing!!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI know this is a standalone but I feel like I can’t fully judge this story properly without having read all the previous books in this world. I feel like I’m missing a lot of background info! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFrom my understanding, this world starts with Jill’s \u003ci\u003eFive Families\u003c/i\u003e series (which I did ARC read the first 4 books years ago- don’t really remember them tbh but from my reviews I enjoyed them), and then there’s \u003ci\u003eThe Byrne Brothers\u003c/i\u003e (which I haven't read), and now this new series, \u003ci\u003eMoretti Men\u003c/i\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eanyway!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhere do I start!?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSante and Amelie are such amazing characters. Their love story began four years ago, though neither realized it at the time. After leaving for Sicily, Sante returns to his family—the Italian mafia—unsure of where he belongs or if he even fits in anymore. For two weeks, he keeps his return a secret, hesitant to commit to staying until he’s sure his feelings for Amelie are real and sustainable. He met her at a wedding when they were both teenagers, already scarred by loss and hardship. Yet even in the darkness, Amelie was his light. Though she didn’t know it then, she became the reason he wanted to change.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAmelie, a dedicated ballerina, pours her heart into perfecting her art, practicing for hours every day. Fiercely loyal to her sister and her niece Violet, Amelie is deeply rooted in her small family—the only family she has left. Her sister’s marriage ties them to the Irish mafia, creating a bond of loyalty and trust between the two families.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut Amelie carries a heavy secret, one that could put lives at risk if it were revealed. She isolates herself to protect those she loves, unable to form meaningful relationships. She channels all her energy into dancing, finding solace in the solitude of late-night rehearsals at the theater.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003e“There’s a peacefulness in dancing by myself. A solitude I know all too well… which is how I can tell the second I’m no longer alone. I feel it now. Someone else is in the theater. They’re watching me from the shadows.” \u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe suspense in this book is masterfully done. From Sante’s initial secretive return and his bold decision to stalk Amelie in the shadows, to the moment she discovers his true identity at a family dinner, the tension was palpable. And let’s not forget the twists and turns! Just when I thought I had things figured out, Jill Ramsower threw in surprises that left my head spinning.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI wasn't sure how I felt about the whole stalking aspect of the story. It felt weird, and I felt like she forgave him way too quickly. But besides that, their love is raw, intense, and unforgettable. Together, they prove that even the most shattered pieces can come together to form something extraordinary. Sante’s protectiveness and devotion, paired with Amelie’s vulnerability and strength, made for a love story that was both tender and fiery. The way he worshipped her, the way she softened for him—it was perfection.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003e“Who did I say this body belongs to?”\u003cbr /\u003e“You,” I breathe.\u003cbr /\u003e“And that’s the problem. How will anyone else unlock a door when I’m the only one with the key?” \u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOverall, I loved getting back into this world, and I just love Jill's writing. Although I felt like I was missing some things Devil’s Thirst is a journey of healing, redemption, and finding love when you least expect it. I'm eager for the next installment! If you’re a fan of mafia romance with sizzling chemistry, complex characters, and a plot that keeps you guessing, don’t miss this one. Sante and Amelie’s story will stay with me for a long time. Highly recommend!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e────── ✧ ⋆⋅☆⋅⋆ ♡ ⋆⋅☆⋅⋆ ✧ ──────\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e⊹ 𝔀𝓱𝓪𝓽 𝓽𝓸 𝓮𝔁𝓹𝓮𝓬𝓽 ⊹\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e❥Alpha anti-hero\u2028\u003cbr /\u003e❥Ballerina\u003cbr /\u003e❥'Good Girl'\u003cbr /\u003e❥'My Pet'\u003cbr /\u003e❥'My wife'\u003cbr /\u003e❥Medium Burn\u2028\u003cbr /\u003e❥Obsessed stalker\u2028\u003cbr /\u003e❥Touch her and 💀\u2028\u003cbr /\u003e❥Tragic past\u2028\u003cbr /\u003e❥Secret identity\u2028\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003eThank you for the ARC, Jill♡\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e_________________________________\u003cbr /\u003eDevil's Thirst | \u003ca href=\"https://wp.me/p23dZM-5Ps\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eReview\u003c/a\u003e \u003cbr /\u003eDeath’s Favor | \u003ca href=\"https://wp.me/p23dZM-61Y\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eReview\u003c/a\u003e \u003cbr /\u003eMistletoe Masquerade | \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://somanyybookssolittletime.wordpress.com/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eBlog\u003c/a\u003e ಇ \u003ca href=\"https://app.thestorygraph.com/profile/anacarter\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eStoryGraph\u003c/a\u003e ಇ \u003ca href=\"https://www.instagram.com/smbslt_26/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eInstagram\u003c/a\u003e ಇ \u003ca href=\"https://twitter.com/SMBSLT_26\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eTwitter\u003c/a\u003e ಇ \u003ca href=\"https://www.facebook.com/SoManyBooksSoLittleTime/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eFacebook\u003c/a\u003e","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A19R7MNJ1GKII\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz\"}}"},"likeCount":12,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:29897986":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":29897986,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1678235434i/29897986._UX200_CR0,23,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":78,"textReviewsCount":240,"name":"*ೃnaziba ˘͈ᵕ˘͈","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/29897986-naziba","contributor":null,"id":29897986},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A32J8A2MBU0LD9":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A32J8A2MBU0LD9"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A32J8A2MBU0LD9\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A32J8A2MBU0LD9","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A32J8A2MBU0LD9"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default"