a://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.L9U4EDO4TvKdDo4ZxmRjkw","creator":{"__ref":"User:35827872"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1770233191781,"createdAt":1770056246056,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1770057696318,"text":"I was going to give it a 4.75 but than thought nuh, this deserves the full 5 stars. I loved it! It's a kind of a mafia romance but on a softer side with already established world of characters from other connected series, which I actually didn't mind. It only made me want to possibly go back and read up on some of the previous shenanigans. I know I definitely want more on Tommy and his is the next book in the series. Yay! \u003cbr /\u003eNow to the main course - I am totally and unabashedly obsessed with Sante. His devotion to Mellie and the change he made himself go through to be worthy of her is EVERYTHING. And sure he stalked her for a bit, honestly though, it worked for them and that was kind of the whole point that his crazy matched her broken and it became something beautiful. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003ci\u003e\"If I'd known stalkers were so considerate, I would have found one ages ago.\"\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOh the way he heals her. Like I said, obsessed. And then Freya entered the chat and I was like what are you doing to me, you perfect fictional man? If I had to endure some stalking to have someone like Sante on the other end of that - I'm game. Commence with the stalking.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThank you Hambright PR and Jill Ramsower for the copy of this book. All thoughts and opinions are my own.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOver and out","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3DO0RM5LBP2MX\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.rMUquUqxpWpmTijz\"}}"},"likeCount":8,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":4},"User:146873471":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":146873471,"imageUrlSquare":"htt